      "content": "I understand where you're coming from, but it's not about being forced to watch a terrible movie. It's about finding your own meaning in the experience, even if it's not what others see. The struggle, the suffering, it's all part of the human condition. Embracing it, accepting it, that's what makes us human. So, don't walk out. Stay in the theater, feel the emotions, experience the highs and lows. It's in those moments that you truly live. And remember, even in the end, when the movie is over, you're still you. You still exist. So, why not make the most of it? Why not live fully, even if it's just for a little while longer?",
